    {
      "id": "rejudge",
      "type": "uipath.agent.autonomous",
      "typeVersion": "1.4",
      "display": {
        "label": "Agent re-judge",
        "icon": "autonomous-agent"
      },
      "inputs": {
        "systemPrompt": "You are SplitSentinel, a procurement controls analyst.\n\nDecide whether the anchor purchase requisition (PR) and the candidate PRs represent ONE business requirement that was split into several requisitions to avoid an approval tier, a quote requirement or a competitive-bidding (RFQ) requirement.\n\nYou receive: the anchor PR, the candidate PRs (related PRs from the last 30 days), the rule engine's result, the approval matrix, the vendor, the requester, the blanket POs, and optionally the requester's justification. The procurement policy is below. Use ONLY this data and the policy.\n\nHow to decide:\n1. Treat PRs as one requirement when they share a project, event, purpose or delivery window, or when the items are components or accessories of each other (for example laptops, their chargers and their docking stations for the same team). Different vendors do not make them separate.\n2. PRs raised by different requesters in the same cost centre, for the same need from the same vendor, count as one requirement.\n3. Check the legitimate exceptions in the policy: RECURRING, BLANKET_PO, SEPARATE_PROJECT, EMERGENCY, STAGGERED_DELIVERY. Use an exception only when the PR data supports it (for example a SEPARATE_PROJECT needs different projects, sites and purposes; EMERGENCY needs the emergency flag and a specific reason).\n4. If a requester justification is given, judge whether it is specific and consistent with the PR data. Vague reasons (\"urgent\", \"needed quickly\", \"we always order this way\") do not qualify.\n5. When the evidence is mixed, prefer LIKELY_SPLIT with suggestedAction ASK_REQUESTER over NOT_SPLIT. If a justification was already given and the evidence is still mixed, use LIKELY_SPLIT with suggestedAction CONSOLIDATE.\n6. Compute combinedAmount as the sum of the amounts of the PRs you consider one requirement (always include the anchor), and requiredApprovalTier from that amount using the approval matrix (min inclusive, max exclusive).\n\nRules for your answer:\n- relatedPrIds may contain ONLY prId values that appear in the input. Never invent PRs, amounts, dates or facts.\n- reasoning: at most 120 words, citing PR ids and field values.\n- Your reasoning must agree with your verdict and suggestedAction. When a legitimate exception applies, the PRs may be approved separately: do not also say they must be consolidated or re-routed. If you believe consolidation is needed, the verdict is SPLIT or LIKELY_SPLIT, not NOT_SPLIT.\n- If the verdict is NOT_SPLIT, related PRs are just the anchor unless you are explaining an exception, and suggestedAction is APPROVE.\n\nReturn a result conforming to the output schema:\n- verdict: SPLIT, LIKELY_SPLIT or NOT_SPLIT.\n- confidence: a number from 0 to 1.\n- patterns: the pattern codes that apply, from P1 (same requester and vendor), P2 (amounts just under a threshold), P3 (same items), P4 (related items for one need), P5 (several requesters, same cost centre and vendor), P6 (raised close together), P7 (requester habitually near limits).\n- relatedPrIds: the prIds that form the one requirement, including the anchor.\n- combinedAmount: the INR total of relatedPrIds.\n- requiredApprovalTier: T1, T2, T3 or T4 for combinedAmount.\n- competitiveBidRequired: true when that tier requires an RFQ.\n- legitException: NONE, RECURRING, BLANKET_PO, SEPARATE_PROJECT, EMERGENCY or STAGGERED_DELIVERY.\n- reasoning: the short explanation.\n- suggestedAction: CONSOLIDATE, ASK_REQUESTER or APPROVE.\n\nPROCUREMENT POLICY:\n# Procurement Policy — Purchase Requisition Splitting\n\n**Applies to:** all purchase requisitions (PRs) and purchase orders (POs) raised by employees.\n**Owner:** Procurement · **Version:** 1.0\n\n## 1. Approval matrix\n\nEvery requirement is approved at the tier that matches its **total value**.\n\n| Tier | Total value (INR) | Approver | Quotes required | Competitive bid (RFQ) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T1 | below 1,00,000 | Line Manager | 1 | No |\n| T2 | 1,00,000 to below 5,00,000 | Department Head | 3 | No |\n| T3 | 5,00,000 to below 25,00,000 | CFO | 3 | Yes |\n| T4 | 25,00,000 and above | CFO and Procurement Committee | 3 | Yes |\n\n## 2. Splitting is prohibited\n\nDividing a single requirement into several requisitions or orders, so that each one falls below an approval tier or avoids the quote or competitive-bid requirement, is prohibited. This applies whether the split is made by one employee or by several employees acting together.\n\n## 3. What counts as a single requirement\n\nRequisitions are treated as **one requirement** when any of the following is true:\n\n1. They serve the same project, event or business purpose.\n2. They are for the same goods or services from the same vendor, raised within a short period (normally within 30 days).\n3. The items are components or accessories of each other, for example laptops, their chargers and their docking stations for the same team.\n4. They are delivered to the same site in the same delivery window for the same need.\n5. They are raised by different employees in the same cost centre for the same need from the same vendor.\n\nThe **lookback window** for comparing requisitions is **30 days**.\n\n## 4. Legitimate exceptions\n\nThe following are **not** splitting, provided the facts in the requisitions support them:\n\n| Code | Exception | Conditions |\n|---|---|---|\n| RECURRING | Recurring consumables | Routine, periodic purchases (stationery, pantry, cleaning, courier) from a vendor designated as recurring, at normal periodic volumes |\n| BLANKET_PO | Blanket PO call-offs | Each requisition references a valid blanket PO for the same vendor, within its validity dates and approved amount |\n| SEPARATE_PROJECT | Separate requirements | Different projects, cost centres, sites **and** business purposes, each documented on the requisition |\n| EMERGENCY | Documented emergency | Requisitions flagged as emergency with a specific reason (for example equipment breakdown, safety issue). They proceed individually without waiting for combined-tier approval; Procurement reviews the combined value after the fact. |\n| STAGGERED_DELIVERY | Vendor-agreed staggered delivery | One requirement delivered in instalments, where the total was approved at the correct tier |\n\nA justification must be **specific** and consistent with the requisition data. General reasons such as \"urgent\", \"needed quickly\" or \"we always order this way\" do not qualify.\n\n## 5. Consequence\n\nWhen requisitions are found to be one requirement:\n\n1. They are consolidated and routed to the approver for the **combined** value.\n2. Quote and competitive-bid requirements apply to the combined value.\n3. Repeated splitting by the same employee (three or more confirmed cases within 90 days) is reported to Internal Audit.\n\n",
        "userPrompt": "Case data:\n{{ $vars.rules.output.agentInput }}\n\nRequester justification:\n{{ $vars.justification }}",
        "model": "anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6",
        "mode": "standard",
        "temperature": 0,
        "maxTokenPerResponse": 16384,
        "maxIterations": 25,
        "isConversational": false,
        "guardrails": [],
        "name": "rejudge",
        "agentInputVariables": [
          {
            "id": "rules__output__agentInput",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=js:$vars.rules.output.agentInput"
          },
          {
            "id": "justification",
            "type": "string",
            "binding": "=js:$vars.justification"
          }
        ],
        "agentOutputVariables": [
          {
            "id": "verdict",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "id": "confidence",
            "type": "number"
          },
          {
            "id": "patterns",
            "type": "array"
          },
          {
            "id": "relatedPrIds",
            "type": "array"
          },
          {
            "id": "combinedAmount",
            "type": "number"
          },
          {
            "id": "requiredApprovalTier",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "id": "competitiveBidRequired",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          {
            "id": "legitException",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "id": "reasoning",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "id": "suggestedAction",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ],
        "source": "9cc680e9-471b-4f63-90bd-30d915db5c8f",
        "errorHandlingEnabled": true
      },
      "outputs": {
        "error": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Error information if the node fails",
          "source": "=Error",
          "var": "error",
          "schema": {
            "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "code",
              "message",
              "detail",
              "category",
              "status"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "code": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Error code as a string"
              },
              "message": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "High-level error message"
              },
              "detail": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Detailed error description"
              },
              "category": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Error category"
              },
              "status": {
                "type": "integer",
                "description": "HTTP status code"
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        }
      },
      "uniqueId": "5e737b6e-65fb-4b68-9326-89de446348b6"
    },
    {
      "id": "check3",
      "type": "core.action.script",
      "typeVersion": "1.1",
      "display": {
        "label": "Re-validate",
        "icon": "code"
      },
      "inputs": {
        "script": "\n// SplitSentinel rule engine.\n// Pure function, no I/O. The Flow's rule-engine script node inlines this file's source,\n// so keep it plain ES2019 (no imports, no top-level await) and change it only here.\n\nvar DAY_MS = 86400000;\nvar LOOKBACK_DAYS = 30;\nvar HISTORY_DAYS = 90;\nvar NEAR_LIMIT_MIN = 0.85;\nvar HABIT_MIN = 0.9;\nvar BURST_HOURS = 72;\nvar SIMILARITY_MIN = 0.7;\nvar EXCLUDED_STATUSES = ['Draft', 'Rejected'];\nvar STOPWORDS = ['and', 'for', 'the', 'with', 'from', 'pcs', 'nos', 'qty', 'units', 'set', 'of'];\n\nfunction num(x) {\n  var n = Number(x);\n  return isFinite(n) ? n : 0;\n}\n\nfunction ts(x) {\n  var t = Date.parse(x);\n  return isFinite(t) ? t : 0;\n}\n\nfunction sameText(a, b) {\n  return a != null && b != null && String(a).trim() !== '' && String(a).trim().toLowerCase() === String(b).trim().toLowerCase();\n}\n\nfunction sortedTiers(matrix) {\n  return (matrix || []).slice().sort(function (a, b) { return num(a.minAmount) - num(b.minAmount); });\n}\n\nfunction tierFor(amount, matrix) {\n  var tiers = sortedTiers(matrix);\n  for (var i = 0; i < tiers.length; i++) {\n    var max = tiers[i].maxAmount;\n    var hasMax = max !== null && max !== undefined && max !== '';\n    if (amount >= num(tiers[i].minAmount) && (!hasMax || amount < num(max))) {\n      return { tier: tiers[i], index: i };\n    }\n  }\n  return { tier: null, index: -1 };\n}\n\n// Ratio of amount to the nearest ceiling above it: its tier's upper bound or the requester's limit.\nfunction ceilingRatio(amount, matrix, requesterLimit) {\n  var best = 0;\n  var t = tierFor(amount, matrix).tier;\n  if (t && t.maxAmount !== null && t.maxAmount !== undefined && t.maxAmount !== '') {\n    best = Math.max(best, amount / num(t.maxAmount));\n  }\n  var limit = num(requesterLimit);\n  if (limit > 0 && amount <= limit) best = Math.max(best, amount / limit);\n  return best;\n}\n\nfunction tokens(text) {\n  return String(text || '').toLowerCase().split(/[^a-z0-9]+/).filter(function (w) {\n    return w.length > 2 && !/^\\d+$/.test(w) && STOPWORDS.indexOf(w) < 0;\n  });\n}\n\nfunction jaccard(a, b) {\n  var sa = {}, sb = {}, inter = 0, union = 0, k;\n  tokens(a).forEach(function (w) { sa[w] = true; });\n  tokens(b).forEach(function (w) { sb[w] = true; });\n  for (k in sa) { union++; if (sb[k]) inter++; }\n  for (k in sb) { if (!sa[k]) union++; }\n  return union === 0 ? 0 : inter / union;\n}\n\nfunction isCandidate(anchor, pr) {\n  if (sameText(pr.vendorId, anchor.vendorId) && sameText(pr.requesterId, anchor.requesterId)) return true;\n  if (sameText(pr.vendorId, anchor.vendorId) && sameText(pr.costCenter, anchor.costCenter)) return true;\n  if (sameText(pr.projectCode, anchor.projectCode)) return true;\n  if (sameText(pr.requesterId, anchor.requesterId) && sameText(pr.category, anchor.category)) return true;\n  return false;\n}\n\nfunction validBlanket(ref, vendorId, atTime, blanketPos) {\n  for (var i = 0; i < (blanketPos || []).length; i++) {\n    var b = blanketPos[i];\n    if (sameText(b.blanketPoId, ref) && sameText(b.vendorId, vendorId)\n      && atTime >= ts(b.validFrom) && atTime <= ts(b.validTo) + DAY_MS - 1) return true;\n  }\n  return false;\n}\n\n/**\n * @param anchor  the PR being checked\n * @param prs     PRs created in the 90 days before the anchor (any requester); the anchor itself is ignored\n * @param ctx     { approvalMatrix, requester, vendor, blanketPos }\n */\nfunction scorePrs(anchor, prs, ctx) {\n  ctx = ctx || {};\n  var matrix = ctx.approvalMatrix || [];\n  var requester = ctx.requester || {};\n  var vendor = ctx.vendor || {};\n  var anchorTime = ts(anchor.createdAt);\n  var anchorAmount = num(anchor.amount);\n  var requesterLimit = num(requester.approvalLimit);\n\n  var prior = (prs || []).filter(function (p) {\n    var t = ts(p.createdAt);\n    return !sameText(p.prId, anchor.prId) && t <= anchorTime && t >= anchorTime - HISTORY_DAYS * DAY_MS\n      && EXCLUDED_STATUSES.indexOf(String(p.status)) < 0;\n  });\n  var candidates = prior.filter(function (p) {\n    return ts(p.createdAt) >= anchorTime - LOOKBACK_DAYS * DAY_MS && isCandidate(anchor, p);\n  });\n  var group = [anchor].concat(candidates);\n  var combined = group.reduce(function (s, p) { return s + num(p.amount); }, 0);\n  var anchorTier = tierFor(anchorAmount, matrix);\n  var combinedTier = tierFor(combined, matrix);\n  var crossesTier = combinedTier.index > anchorTier.index;\n  var exceedsRequesterLimit = requesterLimit > 0 && anchorAmount <= requesterLimit && combined > requesterLimit;\n\n  var signals = [];\n  function add(code, points, detail) { signals.push({ code: code, points: points, detail: detail }); }\n\n  if (candidates.length > 0) {\n    var p1 = candidates.filter(function (p) { return sameText(p.vendorId, anchor.vendorId) && sameText(p.requesterId, anchor.requesterId); });\n    if (p1.length) add('P1', 25, 'Same requester and vendor: ' + p1.map(function (p) { return p.prId; }).join(', '));\n\n    var p5 = candidates.filter(function (p) {\n      return sameText(p.vendorId, anchor.vendorId) && !sameText(p.requesterId, anchor.requesterId) && sameText(p.costCenter, anchor.costCenter);\n    });\n    if (p5.length) add('P5', 15, 'Same vendor and cost centre, different requester: ' + p5.map(function (p) { return p.prId; }).join(', '));\n\n    if (crossesTier || exceedsRequesterLimit) {\n      add('TIER', 20, 'Combined INR ' + combined + ' needs ' + (combinedTier.tier ? combinedTier.tier.tierId : '?')\n        + (crossesTier ? ' (anchor alone: ' + (anchorTier.tier ? anchorTier.tier.tierId : '?') + ')' : '')\n        + (exceedsRequesterLimit ? '; exceeds requester limit INR ' + requesterLimit : ''));\n    }\n\n    var nearAll = group.every(function (p) { return ceilingRatio(num(p.amount), matrix, requesterLimit) >= NEAR_LIMIT_MIN; });\n    if (nearAll) add('P2', 15, 'Every PR is within 85-100% of a threshold');\n\n    var times = group.map(function (p) { return ts(p.createdAt); });\n    if (Math.max.apply(null, times) - Math.min.apply(null, times) <= BURST_HOURS * 3600000) {\n      add('P6', 10, 'All PRs raised within 72 hours');\n    }\n\n    var similar = candidates.every(function (p) { return jaccard(p.description, anchor.description) >= SIMILARITY_MIN; });\n    if (similar) add('P3', 10, 'Near-identical item descriptions');\n\n    var sameProject = anchor.projectCode && group.every(function (p) { return sameText(p.projectCode, anchor.projectCode); });\n    if (sameProject) add('PROJ', 10, 'All PRs on project ' + anchor.projectCode);\n\n    var habit = prior.filter(function (p) {\n      return sameText(p.requesterId, anchor.requesterId) && ceilingRatio(num(p.amount), matrix, requesterLimit) >= HABIT_MIN;\n    });\n    if (habit.length >= 3) add('P7', 10, habit.length + ' PRs in 90 days at 90-100% of a threshold');\n\n    if (vendor.isRecurring === true || String(vendor.isRecurring).toLowerCase() === 'true') {\n      add('X_RECURRING', -20, 'Vendor ' + (vendor.name || anchor.vendorId) + ' is a recurring-spend vendor');\n    }\n\n    var blanketRef = anchor.blanketPoRef;\n    var allBlanket = blanketRef && group.every(function (p) {\n      return sameText(p.blanketPoRef, blanketRef) && validBlanket(blanketRef, p.vendorId, ts(p.createdAt), ctx.blanketPos);\n    });\n    if (allBlanket) add('X_BLANKET', -30, 'All PRs call off valid blanket PO ' + blanketRef);\n\n    var allEmergency = group.every(function (p) { return p.isEmergency === true || String(p.isEmergency).toLowerCase() === 'true'; });\n    if (allEmergency) add('X_EMERGENCY', -10, 'All PRs flagged emergency');\n  }\n\n  var total = signals.reduce(function (s, x) { return s + x.points; }, 0);\n  var score = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, total));\n  var route = score < 30 ? 'RELEASE' : score < 60 ? 'AGENT' : 'AGENT_HUMAN_REQUIRED';\n\n  return {\n    score: score,\n    route: route,\n    patterns: signals.filter(function (x) { return x.points > 0; }).map(function (x) { return x.code; }),\n    signals: signals,\n    groupPrIds: group.map(function (p) { return p.prId; }),\n    combinedAmount: combined,\n    anchorTier: anchorTier.tier ? anchorTier.tier.tierId : null,\n    combinedTier: combinedTier.tier ? combinedTier.tier.tierId : null,\n    crossesTier: crossesTier,\n    requesterLimit: requesterLimit,\n    exceedsRequesterLimit: exceedsRequesterLimit\n  };\n}\n\n\nvar a = null;\ntry { a = $vars.rejudge.output || null; } catch (e) { a = null; }\nvar rules = $vars.rules.output;\nvar errors = [], corrections = [];\nvar VERDICTS = ['SPLIT', 'LIKELY_SPLIT', 'NOT_SPLIT'];\nvar EXCEPTIONS = ['NONE', 'RECURRING', 'BLANKET_PO', 'SEPARATE_PROJECT', 'EMERGENCY', 'STAGGERED_DELIVERY'];\nvar ACTIONS = ['CONSOLIDATE', 'ASK_REQUESTER', 'APPROVE'];\nif (!a || typeof a !== 'object') errors.push('no structured answer returned');\nelse {\n  if (VERDICTS.indexOf(a.verdict) < 0) errors.push('verdict must be one of ' + VERDICTS.join(', '));\n  if (EXCEPTIONS.indexOf(a.legitException) < 0) errors.push('legitException must be one of ' + EXCEPTIONS.join(', '));\n  if (ACTIONS.indexOf(a.suggestedAction) < 0) errors.push('suggestedAction must be one of ' + ACTIONS.join(', '));\n  if (typeof a.reasoning !== 'string' || !a.reasoning.trim()) errors.push('reasoning is required');\n}\nvar ok = errors.length === 0;\nvar fallback = { verdict: 'FAILED', confidence: 0, patterns: [], relatedPrIds: rules.groupPrIds,\n  combinedAmount: rules.combinedAmount, requiredApprovalTier: rules.combinedTier, competitiveBidRequired: false,\n  legitException: 'NONE', reasoning: 'Agent answer invalid: ' + errors.join('; '), suggestedAction: 'CONSOLIDATE' };\nif (!ok) return Object.assign({ ok: false, errors: errors.join('; '), corrections: '' }, true ? fallback : {});\nvar ids = (Array.isArray(a.relatedPrIds) ? a.relatedPrIds : String(a.relatedPrIds || '').split(','))\n  .map(function (x) { return String(x).trim(); }).filter(function (x) { return x; });\nvar known = rules.knownPrIds;\nvar unknown = ids.filter(function (x) { return known.indexOf(x) < 0; });\nif (unknown.length) corrections.push('removed unknown PR ids ' + unknown.join(', '));\nids = ids.filter(function (x) { return known.indexOf(x) >= 0; });\nif (ids.indexOf($vars.prId) < 0) ids.unshift($vars.prId);\nvar amount = ids.reduce(function (s, x) { return s + (rules.amounts[x] || 0); }, 0);\nif (Math.abs(Number(a.combinedAmount) - amount) > 1) corrections.push('combinedAmount ' + a.combinedAmount + ' -> ' + amount);\nvar t = tierFor(amount, rules.matrix).tier || {};\nif (a.requiredApprovalTier !== t.tierId) corrections.push('requiredApprovalTier ' + a.requiredApprovalTier + ' -> ' + t.tierId);\nreturn { ok: true, errors: '', corrections: corrections.join('; '), verdict: a.verdict,\n  confidence: Number(a.confidence) || 0, patterns: Array.isArray(a.patterns) ? a.patterns : [],\n  relatedPrIds: ids, combinedAmount: amount, requiredApprovalTier: t.tierId,\n  competitiveBidRequired: t.rfqRequired === true || String(t.rfqRequired) === 'true',\n  legitException: a.legitException, reasoning: a.reasoning, suggestedAction: a.suggestedAction };\n"
      },
      "outputs": {
        "output": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "The return value of the script",
          "source": "=result.response",
          "var": "output"
        },
        "error": {
